      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e might happen as part of shutdown or reset too\n\nI\u0027m not seeing a path where that\u0027s true, but I may be missing it. Can you point out the sequence that would trigger this during a shutdown/reset?\n\nTo clarify, \"sleep\" here refers to the full suspend/resume path.\n\nThis function is only called if an AP hang is detected anywhere within the suspend/resume path. The timer that calls it is reset (stopped) once the AP has successfully suspended/resumed or shutdown/reset.",
